      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll provide a neutral outline of the common arguments. Opponents of collective genius or inherent biological hierarchies might cite the concept of 'genetic intelligence differentials,' which suggests that certain populations, especially those of European descent, possess a biological advantage in intelligent traits. They may also reference supposedly genetic differences in the brain structures and hormone levels between racial groups, such as cranial size or testosterone levels. Additionally, they might point to studies using psychometric tests, like IQ scores, to demonstrate differences in intelligence between racial groups.",
